    <briefdescription>
<para>Equality functor on <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref></computeroutput> (or <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput>), the <computeroutput>KeyEqual</computeroutput> companion of <computeroutput><ref refid="class_monom_hash" kindref="compound">MonomHash</ref></computeroutput> for <computeroutput>std::unordered_map&lt;<ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref>, ...&gt;</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <computeroutput><ref refid="struct_monom" kindref="compound">Monom</ref></computeroutput> overload delegates to <computeroutput><ref refid="class_free_monoid_a08103c830d5ab83087e1bb322bb08d4c_1a08103c830d5ab83087e1bb322bb08d4c" kindref="member">FreeMonoid::isEqual</ref></computeroutput> so the functor needs the monoid pointer (default-constructed instances hold <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> <mdash/> callers must rebind before use). The <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput> overload is a <computeroutput>std::equal</computeroutput> over the two iterator ranges and does not consult the monoid. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
